The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about `presolve_extract_integer_enforcement` in Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT solver:\n\n`presolve_extract_integer_enforcement` is a boolean parameter with a default value of `false`. This parameter is defined in the SAT solver's parameters configuration file.\n\nThe primary documentation appears in the `sat_parameters.proto` file from the Google OR-Tools repository. When enabled, this parameter extracts from linear constraints enforcement literals of the form \"integer variable at bound => simplified constraint\", which should always be beneficial except that the solver doesn't always handle them as efficiently as it could.\n\nThe parameter is used during the CP-SAT presolve phase, which applies various simplification rules to optimize the model before the actual solving begins. You can find the full definition and usage in the [sat_parameters.proto file](https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto) in the Google OR-Tools GitHub repository.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"bbc7bbd1-b9f3-4b11-8fc1-514abf2449cd","timestamp":"2026-05-07T23:01:57.750Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5ea8858f-f704-4c2c-af53-fd6cb09fb16a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
