{"parentUuid":"ee728778-ef8d-4819-b330-2f665690e6b6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"b9474645-0d56-40f0-a822-a5a662a1bfd0","agentId":"a0b6fa2949affdad1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012WdX3fR8m1tA7aNYYLM6pW","type":"tool_result","content":"4043:  // extracting some of these enforcement, as those can be \"lifted\" booleans. We\n4096:    context_->UpdateRuleStats(\"linear + amo: extracted enforcement literal\",\n4748:  // We can only extract enforcement literals if the maximum coefficient\n4803:    // Lets not split except if we extract enforcement.\n4860:      !context_->params().presolve_extract_integer_enforcement() ||\n4864:  // same time as we extract enforcement literals.\n4913:      context_->UpdateRuleStats(\"linear: extracted enforcement literal\");\n4917:          \"linear: extracted integer enforcement literal\");\n9799:      // If we extracted some enforcement, we redo some presolve.\n11041:            auto extracted = enforcement_vars.extract(implication_lit);","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"43629ea3-61b2-4606-95df-bdff683244bd","timestamp":"2026-05-07T23:02:40.585Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ee728778-ef8d-4819-b330-2f665690e6b6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"43629ea3-61b2-4606-95df-bdff683244bd","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a0b6fa2949affdad1","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01N8ztSYQAFzFf2NFM4o96it","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All evidence collected. Compiling the verdict.\n\n---\n\n## P0 #23 Verification Report — `presolve_extract_integer_enforcement`\n\n### 1. R11 transcript origin (a67cf942cd679915d)\n\nR11 was **about cardinality SAT encoding** (sequential / commander / totalizer / sorting network). The `presolve_extract_integer_enforcement` recommendation was the **#1 of \"Top 3 改进方向\"** at the very end:\n\n> \"做什么：让 presolve 把 OnlyEnforceIf 的 enforcement 从线性约束里抽出来，转成纯 Boolean implication / 收益：100 处里大约 30–50 处会被简化掉 / 期望：5–15% 单 wave 提速；如果触发了之前没触发的简化，可能 2–3x\"\n\n**Crucial finding**: R11 cited NO benchmark, NO CP-SAT team statement, NO MIPLIB result for this number. The \"+5–15% / maybe 2–3x\" is a Claude-side **inference** from \"30–50 处简化\" — pure speculation, not data.\n\n### 2. OR-Tools v9.15 source verification\n\n**Proto** (`sat_parameters.proto` field 174, default `false`):\n```\n// If true, we will extract from linear constraints, enforcement literals of\n// the form \"integer variable at bound => simplified constraint\". This should\n// always be beneficial except that we don't always handle them as efficiently\n// as we could for now. This causes problem on manna81.mps (LP relaxation not\n// as tight it seems) and on neos-3354841-apure.mps.gz (too many literals\n// created this way).\n```\n\n**This is NOT what R11 claims.** R11 said the param \"extracts from OnlyEnforceIf into Boolean implication.\" Source says the opposite direction: it extracts **integer-variable-at-bound implications OUT OF plain linear constraints, AS new enforcement literals** (i.e., it *creates* half-reified constraints, not removes them).\n\n**Implementation** (`cp_model_presolve.cc:4715-4920`, `ExtractEnforcementLiteralFromLinearConstraint`):\n- Already runs by default for **Boolean** terms (the `only_extract_booleans` path)\n- The flag only flips `only_extract_booleans = false`, which then ALSO extracts **integer variable @ bound** terms via `GetOrCreateVarValueEncoding(ref, MinOf(ref))`\n- Logged rule stat: `\"linear: extracted integer enforcement literal\"`\n- Transformation: a term `coeff * X` where `coeff >= threshold` and `X` is an integer var, gets split off — a literal `eq(X, bound)` is created and added to `ct->enforcement_literal()`, and the term is dropped from the linear body. Equivalent to: `[lin <= rhs]` becomes `[X = bound] => [reduced_lin <= rhs]`\n\n**Soundness for max objective**: Sound. The transformation preserves feasibility. But the proto comment explicitly warns of two regressions on MIPLIB: `manna81.mps` (LP relaxation gets *looser*) and `neos-3354841-apure.mps.gz` (literal explosion). For our `max_lex(area, min_side)` master with LP relaxation already loose, the manna81 risk is real.\n\n**Side effects**: \n- `ModelIsExpanded()` short-circuits the integer path even when flag is on (line 4861) — so it only fires in early presolve rounds before constraint expansion\n- Creates new `var_value_encoding` literals → linearization_level=1 LP gets more variables but possibly weaker bounds\n- Triggers `some_integer_encoding_were_extracted` flag (line 4862) which redoes presolve\n\n### 3. Interactions with other params\n\n- **`cp_model_presolve` (default true)**: hard prerequisite. Off → never fires.\n- **`linearization_level`**: param `0/1/2` directly affected. Higher level + flag-on means the new var_value encodings flood the LP. Combined risk of looser relaxation per the proto warning.\n- **`boolean_encoding_level`**: orthogonal — that flag controls full encoding of integer vars; this flag is just one specific extraction site.\n- **`presolve_use_bva`**: independent.\n- **No known mutual-exclusion** in source. No `CHECK` or `if` that turns one off when the other is on.\n- **A/B observability**: Yes — set `log_search_progress=true` and grep `presolve_log` for rule stats `\"linear: extracted integer enforcement literal\"` and `\"linear: extracted enforcement literal\"`. Both increment `UpdateRuleStats` and appear in the final presolve summary table. Diff between flag-on and flag-off runs makes the count directly observable.\n\n### 4. Applicability to our setup\n\nOur 100 OnlyEnforceIf are **already half-reified at construction** (Python `OnlyEnforceIf` calls). The flag does NOT touch existing enforcement_literal — it only creates *new* ones from plain (non-enforced) linear constraints with at-bound integer terms. So:\n\n- The \"30–50 处会被简化\" claim in R11 is **semantically wrong** — the param doesn't simplify our 52 `exact_coordinate_master.py` OnlyEnforceIf at all\n- It might fire on the underlying *plain* linear constraints (e.g., area objective bounds, min_side constraints) where some integer var sits at its bound coefficient threshold — but those are few in our model\n- The \"+5–15%\" number has zero benchmarking provenance — it was a vibes estimate\n\n### Verdict\n\n**P0 #23 verdict = REFUTED**\n\nReasoning:\n1. R11's stated mechanism (\"simplifies our OnlyEnforceIf\") is **factually wrong** per source\n2. R11's \"+5–15% / 2-3x\" had no citation; just inference\n3. Proto comment explicitly warns of **regression cases** (manna81 LP, neos literal explosion)\n4. The param fires only on plain linear constraints with at-bound integer-var-of-large-coefficient — our master is dominated by Boolean placement vars, so applicability is small\n5. Our 100 explicit `OnlyEnforceIf` are unaffected\n\n**Should we keep as P0?** No — **demote to P3 (cheap experiment, low priority)**. It's one parameter line so cost is trivial, but expected value is small or negative. It belongs alongside other \"speculative single-knob\" experiments, not in the P0 batch with shared_tree (already REFUTED) and UNSAT subsolver (PARTIALLY_REFUTED).\n\n**Recommended config**: keep `presolve_extract_integer_enforcement = false` (default). Only revisit if our presolve log shows non-trivial `\"linear: extracted enforcement literal\"` rule stats — meaning the Boolean half is firing a lot, suggesting integer half might also have hits.\n\n**A/B test design (only if user insists on running experiment)**:\n- Hardware budget: 5 wave pairs (10 wave runs total, ~2 hours on 8-worker machine)\n- Setup: identical campaign seed, identical master state, fix `random_seed`, run 5 waves with flag=true and 5 with flag=false on adjacent candidate frontier slices\n- Metrics: (a) wall time per wave, (b) `presolved.num_constraints` post-presolve, (c) `presolved.num_variables`, (d) rule stats `\"linear: extracted integer enforcement literal\"` count (must be > 0 or experiment is null), (e) LP relaxation gap at root, (f) Benders iterations to first feasible\n- **Significance gate**: paired t-test on wall time, p < 0.05 with ≥10% mean delta. If delta < 5% in either direction, declare INSIGNIFICANT and keep default\n- **Stat (d)** is the load-bearing one — if it's near zero, the param literally didn't do anything and (a) variance is just noise\n\n**Pattern update**: parameter-level P0 救火率 now **3/3** — R11's #23 also REFUTED. Strongly recommend treating any future P0 with provenance \"Claude inference based on Top-N speculation\" as P3 by default.\n\n### Key file paths (absolute)\n- `D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\docs\\research\\agent_transcripts\\a67cf942cd679915d.output` (R11 transcript)\n- v9.15 source: `https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/v9.15/ortools/sat/cp_model_presolve.cc#L4715-L4920` (the function)\n- v9.15 source: `https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/v9.15/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto` (field 174)\n- `D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\src\\models\\exact_coordinate_master.py` (52 unaffected OnlyEnforceIf)\n- `D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\src\\models\\routing_subproblem.py` (2 unaffected OnlyEnforceIf)\n- `D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\src\\models\\master_model.py` (1 unaffected OnlyEnforceIf)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":720,"cache_read_input_tokens":64455,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":720,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Cap3R9ruMJQqX49L5hALi","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"162293c1-89c3-4e96-addb-e4941793c2a1","timestamp":"2026-05-07T23:03:41.288Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
